0.516.47However, the combination of Gillian and Stivoric does not disclose or suggest "wherein an amount of time between when the native sensor data representative of the activity of the user that is associated with the second apparatus comprising the health or fitness tracker application begins to not be provided to the second apparatus or when the native sensor data representative of the activity of the user begins to be unavailable to the second apparatus comprising the health or fitness tracker application, and when the pseudo sensor data begins to be provided to the second apparatus using the first apparatus comprising the radio frequency based tracker, is less than a threshold amount of time" as now claimed.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.8336.50However, Stivoric and Gillian together do not describe implementation of providing a continuous stream of data.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
3.4376.507As shown above, the native sensor data stops being provided by the health and fitness tracker 104 at time ti, and the pseudo sensor data starts to be provided by the radio frequency based tracker at time t2, where t2 minus ti is less than t3 minus ti, where t3 minus ti is the threshold amount of time. In another case, as described in Applicant's filed specification at page 8, lines 11-17, at time t3 (or slightly before t3), the health and fitness tracker may send a trigger message to the radio frequency based tracker with an indication to begin providing the pseudo sensor data, such that the trigger message is sent based on the threshold amount of time as for example time t3 minus ti.
